type":"text","url":"/docs/themes/winui#the-shared-values","content":"<ThemeTokens id=\"winui\" group=\"shared\" />"},"2383":{"id":"/docs/themes/winui-13","page_id":"/docs/themes/winui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/themes/winui#finishes","content":"<ThemeFinishes id=\"winui\" />"},"2384":{"id":"/docs/themes","page_id":"/docs/themes","type":"page","content":"Themes","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/themes"},"2385":{"id":"/docs/themes-0","page_id":"/docs/themes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/themes","content":"The palettes the demos can draw in: what a theme is, the radius layers, and a page for each palette."},"2386":{"id":"/docs/themes-1","page_id":"/docs/themes","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/themes#one-look-more-than-one-palette","content":"One look, more than one palette"},"2387":{"id":"/docs/themes-2","page_id":"/docs/themes","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/themes#radii-by-role","content":"Radii by role"},"2388":{"id":"/docs/themes-3","page_id":"/docs/themes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/themes#one-look-more-than-one-palette","content":"A theme is one `AppTheme`: `theme.json` (base tokens: colours, three `radius-*` layer lengths, and fonts),\n`semantics.json` (cross-platform semantics: style groups and `shared` + sparse `light` / `dark`\nfinishes, referencing tokens with `{token}`) and the `index.ts` that names it. An app is _built_\nwith one theme and can _carry_ more, switching between them while it runs with `selectTheme`."},"2389":{"id":"/docs/themes-4","page_id":"/docs/themes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/themes#one-look-more-than-one-palette","content":"Every demo on this site can be drawn in any of these palettes: pick one with the **Demo theme**\nswitch in the nav, and the previews load again in it. The panel above is the showcase — buttons, a\ncard with a field, badges, switches, a slider and a progress bar, with the card, inset and press finishes\nthe palette brings. The list is `apps/website/demos/palettes.ts`. Each palette has its own page,\nwith the same sections: how to install it, every token it sets, and every finish it draws. Those\npages read each theme's `theme.json` and `semantics.json`, following the\ndesign-semantics standard\nand the theme roles spec."},"2390":{"id":"/docs/themes-5","page_id":"/docs/themes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/themes#radii-by-role","content":"`theme.json` states one corner radius per layer in `cssVars.theme` — `radius-control` (in-page\nelements), `radius-container` (cards, menus, popovers, toasts) and `radius-modal` (dialogs, sheets) —\nand `semantics.json`'s `shape.*` references them with `{radius-…}`. `shape.corners.button` makes\nbuttons capsules (`apple`, `material`) or gives them `control` (the rest). A surface nested in\nanother takes the concentric corner, `rounded(outer, inset)`. Every corner that reads a theme radius\nuses `shape.curve` (`\"continuous\"` or `\"circular\"`), which `rounded()` applies in one place."},"2391":{"id":"/docs/themes-6","page_id":"/docs/themes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/themes#radii-by-role","content":"<ThemeIndex />"}},"count":2391},"sorting":{"language":"multilingual","sortableProperties":["content","page_id","type","url"],"sortablePropertiesWithTypes":{"content":"string","page_id":"string","type":"string","url":"string"},"sorts":{"content":{"docs":{"1":1297,"2":1469,"3":1629,"4":1114,"5":1750,"6":2361,"7":1399,"8":1605,"9":1269,"10":1891,"11":186,"12":9,"13":2388,"14":351,"15":361,"16":359,"17":358,"18":348,"19":1734,"20":1624,"21":1612,"22":1380,"23":1773,"24":352,"25":350,"26":360,"27":362,"28":344,"29":899,"30":2069,"31":1780,"32":1753,"33":353,"34":363,"35":345,"36":10,"37":1841,"38":354,"39":346,"40":1316,"41":355,"42":347,"43":2386,"44":334,"45":333,"46":332,"47":1467,"48":2079,"49":2160,"50":1270,"51":1961,"52":342,"53":356,"54":1892,"55":343,"56":349,"57":357,"58":184,"59":1108,"60":1751,"61":1637,"62":2200,"63":1320,"64":1474,"65":1412,"66":1090,"67":