ar's type and a chevron after it — the theme's smallest\nicon, an indicator's."],[66,"A trigger of its own"],[585,"A trigger of your own"],[1433,"A trigger of your own"],[2061,"A trigger of your own"],[913,"A trigger of your own, or a disabled one"],[1604,"A trigger that takes the room of a row"],[287,"A turn that acts"],[1270,"A turn that fails leaves two marks. The sent turn keeps its place, with a `Spinner` and\n`Waiting for a connection` in its footer while the app retries. The assistant's turn holds a\ndestructive `Alert`: an `AlertCircle`, `AlertTitle` naming the failure, and an `AlertDescription`\nwhose `Retry` button asks for the turn again."],[1761,"A turning ring: work going on."],[2000,"A two-state button, in two variants and three sizes, and a group of them."],[947,"A unit after the control"],[1378,"A verdict tints every cell of the whole code."],[141,"A view has no selector for its children, and a child cannot be asked what it is, so the text keeps\nthat gutter either way: an alert without an icon starts 12 points in from its padding. Write the\nicon first — it is what takes the leading column."],[321,"A view styles itself and not its children, so each button wears its own place in the group:\n`item(orientation, position)` squares the sides that touch and keeps one edge per join (the one\nbefore it), the outer sides keeping the corners and the edge the button came with. `first` at the leading edge, `last` at the\ntrailing one, `middle` between two others."],[2102,"A virtualized tree with chevrons and folder icons."],[536,"A week's page"],[1970,"A window with `frame: \"none\"` has no title bar and no border: the app draws the bar, the lights\nand the edges itself. `WindowControls` puts the platform's three buttons at the leading end, the\napp's own content after them."],[318,"A word and a divider"],[59,"Accordion"],[1986,"Action"],[91,"Action sheet"],[179,"Actions"],[1259,"Actions"],[741,"Actions on a change"],[4,"add"],[2152,"Add"],[2043,"Add `ToolbarOverflow` and wrap foldable tools in `ToolbarButton` so the bar measures each item with\n`onLayout` and folds lower-priority tools into the `\"⋯\"` menu as the bar narrows. Give a\n`ToolbarGroup` `fold=\"unit\"` (the default) to fold the whole group together under its\n`accessibilityLabel`, or `fold=\"none\"` to let its `ToolbarButton`s fold individually by their own\n`priority`. The bar draws the hairline rules between visible units and hides until its initial\nmeasurements arrive."],[2279,"Add a colour the app's own classes use (both appearances — a token in one alone is not a token):"],[2149,"Add shadcn-nsh to an existing NSH app."],[2288,"Add the theme to an app with `shadcn-nsh add theme` (or let `init` do it); subsequent `add` runs key-merge missing entries into `theme.json` and `semantics.json` while keeping your values."],[949,"Addons over and under the control"],[2134,"After an update"],[87,"Against `Dialog`"],[779,"Against `Sheet`"],[120,"Alert"],[81,"Alert Dialog"],[282,"Alignment"],[1252,"Alignment"],[1838,"Alone"],[559,"Alpha"],[1420,"Also export `Legend` for a colored square and label beside a chart."],[1539,"Also export `resizableHandleLook`, `resizableHandle`, and `handleThumb` for custom layouts."],[844,"Also exports `emojiGroups`, `emojiGroupLabels` and `emojiPickerClasses` for custom layouts."],[1026,"An `Item` is layout only: it draws a row and takes no presses, so the container decides what a row\ndoes. For a row that is a control — hover fill, keyboard focus, disabled — use the same content on\n`listRow` instead, or wrap it in a view with `onPress` and `role=\"button\"`. `ItemGroup` is\n`role=\"list\"`, but NSH has no `listitem` role, so an `Item` is a plain view and a reader moves\nthrough its text element by element: when the rows can be pressed, mark the pressable view\n`role=\"button\"` and give it an `accessibilityLabel` that says the whole row (or use `listRow`,\nwhich does)."],[537,"An action in the bar"],[1695,"An action is always there: hover alone is something a touch screen has no way to do."],[1671,"An action, a badge"],[1990,"An action's `onClick` runs when it is pressed, and `onDismiss` hears that action's label — or `null` when the toast leaves any other way."],[946,"An addon before and after the input"],[2076,"An agent's steps, one line each — reasoning, a tool call, a source, a failed step — where a line can open onto what it did."],[106,"An app that wants the choice before it draws anything else — `await`, then act — shows the same box\nwith `nsh/base`'s own `AlertDialog.show`, which resolves with `{ action }`. That is the app's call.\nThe parts above declare a box under a root of the page's, for an alert that is part of what the page\ndraws; the library has no imperative `show` of its own: a web alert is\nalways the app's own drawing, and a second way in would be two APIs for one box."],[1907,"An app whose window is the terminal"],[2158,"An app with `nsh.json` (from `nsh init`) is ready:"],[2273,"An app's `nsh.json` sets the look in two places, and the two do not merge:"],[1661,"An app's navigation column beside its page — folded to a strip of icons, or sliding in as a sheet on a phone."],[797,"An editor on the field's well, with line numbers, diagnostics and a find bar."],[892,"An error is announced where the platform does it by itself. `FieldError` is a view with\n`role=\"alert\"` (macOS and the web read it when it appears) and TalkBack's live region\n(`accessibilityLiveRegion: \"assertive\"` on Android). iOS has no live region: `UIAccessibility`'s\nannouncement is the app's call, and NSH does not expose it — put the message in the control's\n`accessibilityHint` there as well if it must be heard the moment it appears. Mark the control\ninvalid, not just the field: pass `invalid` to the control (an `Input`, a `Select`'s trigger),\nbecause `role=\"alert\"` tells a reader that something is wrong, not which field."],[2150,"An existing NSH app"],[1937,"An extension claims a Markdown shape for the app. A `language` claims a fence; `renderCustom`\nreceives the node, with `node.text` the fence's source, and returns the view to draw in its place.\nHere a `chart` fence lists `label value` lines and becomes bars in the theme's brand color."],[1557,"An extension's node view: `addNodeView` returns the app's own component, and the editor draws\nevery node of that type with it — the component runs when a node appears, and its props change in\nplace when the node's attributes or its selection do. `RichNodeViewProps` carries `node` (its\n`attrs`), `selected` (it takes presses, so the caret steps over an atom as one character and\nBackspace deletes it) and the session's own `updateAttributes` / `deleteNode` for a node that edits\nitself. Typing never runs the component."],[137,"An icon and a title are a notice of one line."],[1040,"An icon's tile is `controlSize.control + 12` square and an image's frame `controlSize.row - 8`,\nboth of the theme's control corners, so both grow on a touch screen. `itemLook()` is exported for a\nrow the app draws itself: the same look without the parts. `muted`'s fill is the theme's `muted`\ntoken (`token(\"muted\")`); `default` and `outline` draw what they always did."],[928,"An image viewer"],[1939,"An inline extension replaces each match of its `pattern` with the node the app draws. Keep the\nchip's `verticalAlign` at `middle` and its height under the line height, so the paragraph's lines\nkeep their spacing; `styles.root.lineHeight` gives the chip the room it needs."],[2029,"An inset track of tools, with groups and hairline separators."],[1830,"An on / off switch whose knob springs across a sunk track."],[777,"Another edge"],[342,"Any content"],[640,"Any view can be the trigger; the menu opens at the pointer on a secondary click or a long press."],[1272,"Anything else in `MessageFooter` is drawn as given: a row of `IconButton`s, a retry, an error."],[69,"API"],[94,"API"],[133,"API"],[162,"API"],[182,"API"],[217,"API"],[237,"API"],