ng, with the rail's\nthickness, the band around it, the pressed size, and a vertical rail 128 points long (144 on a\ntouch screen) on every form."],[2260,"Both follow `selectTheme` and the appearance, and with `material: null` the view is drawn as before. The library's own popovers, hover cards, toasts, the editor's find bar and a glass carousel arrow spread it; the popups of `Menu`, `Select` and `Popover` on `nsh/base` take only `popupStyle`, so there the glass keys apply and the platform props do not."],[1922,"Brand-colored links and a pulsing streaming caret."],[245,"Breadcrumb"],[214,"Broken image"],[275,"Bubble"],[9,"build"],[50,"Builds a registry into one JSON per item plus the `index.json` that `list` and `add --all` read."],[341,"Busy"],[331,"Button"],[349,"Button"],[310,"Button group"],[1202,"Buttons"],[950,"Buttons in a group"],[311,"Buttons joined into one control, in a row or a column."],[393,"Calendar"],[1407,"Candles with volume"],[500,"Cap the height with `maxHeight` in `style` on `CodeBlockContent`; the code scrolls inside the block. `wrap` wraps long lines instead of scrolling them sideways, and suits output and errors."],[1964,"Caption buttons"],[438,"Caption over a photo"],[406,"Card"],[711,"Card and backdrop"],[431,"Carousel"],[2280,"Change a role: `primary` in `cssVars.light` and `cssVars.dark`. Change a radius: `radius-control`, `radius-container` or `radius-modal` in `cssVars.theme` (keep `radius` equal to `radius-control`) — every corner follows them: `shape.*` and `rounded()` in the styles, and `rounded-(--radius…)` in the classes, this library's and the app's own alike. Fonts are the app's own: see Fonts."],[2146,"Change the shell to change which props a component takes, which parts it exports, and how they nest. A new prop is read in the shell and passed to the base control; keep the caller's `style`, `hoverStyle` and other style props after the look's, so they still win. Behavior — keyboard, focus, dismissal — stays in `nsh/base`; the shell passes its props through. See nsh.dev/elements."],[2144,"Change the values in that function — a height, a radius, a hover fill — and the shell below still spreads the result. Keep the props it returns; they are what the base control reads. `buttonLook` is one; `iconButtonLook`, `roundButtonLook` and `splitButtonLook` live in the same file, and other components name theirs the same way (`switchLook`, `checkboxLook`). Controls whose shape and dimensions vary by platform (`checkbox`, `switch`, `slider`, `radio-group`, `progress`, `spinner`, `calendar`, `sheet`, and shared `lib/indicator.ts` for fields) read the four control dimensions the theme states through `control()`; the per-component geometry that hangs off them stays right inside those component or lib files."],[2189,"Changing them"],[1396,"Chart colors, grid, cross line and tooltip for nsh/base/plot."],[457,"Checkbox"],[1131,"Checkbox and radio"],[465,"Checked and indeterminate"],[2011,"Chips"],[583,"Chips in the field"],[690,"Clearable, and a placeholder"],[1,"CLI"],[520,"Closed"],[710,"Closing"],[1683,"Closing takes the room away at once: the platform transitions colors, opacity and transforms, not\nlayout, so there is no 200 ms width animation to land (and no `motion-reduce` to switch off) — the\ncolumn is either as wide as its state says, or gone."],[477,"Code, a command's output or a log in a block, with a title, a copy button, line numbers and a footer."],[476,"CodeBlock"],[513,"Collapsible"],[530,"CollapsingHeader"],[553,"ColorPicker"],[2218,"Colors"],[2131,"Colors, radii and shadows"],[665,"Columns"],[574,"Combobox"],[608,"Command"],[1207,"Commands"],[2151,"Commands"],[911,"Compact"],[1386,"Compact"],[1430,"Compact"],[40,"Compares the app's installed files with the registry's. Exits `1` when they differ, `2` when it could not compare."],[2120,"Components"],[2276,"Components take their look from `\"theme\"`: `colors`, `finish`, `shape` and `font` read the tokens where they are used. `\"tailwind\"` shapes class names — which this library writes too (`bg-muted`, `text-sm`, `h-8`) — but it is fixed at build time, so nothing in it can follow `setTheme`. NSH's theme tokens has the rule in full."],[656,"Components: a page named in one of them is aligned with an NSH\nelement, and a page named in none is this library's own. `bun run check:pages` fails when an\nofficial component has no row, when a row names a page that does not exist, and when a row serves\nnothing without saying why."],[63,"Composition"],[85,"Composition"],[124,"Composition"],[174,"Composition"],[210,"Composition"],[249,"Composition"],[279,"Composition"],[314,"Composition"],[410,"Composition"],[435,"Composition"],[480,"Composition"],[517,"Composition"],[534,"Composition"],[578,"Composition"],[631,"Composition"],[684,"Composition"],[703,"Composition"],[773,"Composition"],[800,"Composition"],[849,"Composition"],[875,"Composition"],[909,"Composition"],[943,"Composition"],[1012,"Composition"],[1045,"Composition"],[1103,"Composition"],[1129,"Composition"],[1165,"Composition"],[1197,"Composition"],[1250,"Composition"],[1291,"Composition"],[1329,"Composition"],[1427,"Composition"],[1473,"Composition"],[1494,"Composition"],[1530,"Composition"],[1582,"Composition"],[1598,"Composition"],[1640,"Composition"],[1664,"Composition"],[1776,"Composition"],[1804,"Composition"],[1866,"Composition"],[1887,"Composition"],[1961,"Composition"],[2003,"Composition"],[2032,"Composition"],[2056,"Composition"],[2079,"Composition"],[1863,"Composition parts for a bordered table card using the shared data-table classes."],[2160,"Consumer monorepo scaffolding (`shadcn-nsh create`) is not built. `init` and `add` work in a workspace that already has `apps/*` and a `packages/ui` named `@workspace/ui` (or already holding `nsh-ui.json`)."],[1027,"Contacts as `ItemGroup` rows inside a `List` (`nsh`'s virtualized list), with a heading per letter that sticks to the top until the next one pushes it out. Rows are made as they scroll in, so the list can be as long as the data. `stickyHeaderIndices` names the heading rows; a heading needs an opaque background (the surface's own), or the rows show through it while it sticks."],[1431,"Content with its own frame"],[627,"Context Menu"],[68,"Controlled"],[93,"Controlled"],[398,"Controlled"],[712,"Controlled"],[1781,"Controlled"],[807,"Controlled text"],[22,"Copies items and their `registryDependencies` into the app, dependencies first."],[1928,"Copy on code blocks"],[2121,"Copy-into-app components for Native Shell, built on nsh/base."],[648,"Coverage"],[2126,"Coverage: a page registered in one of its NSH rows is\nBase, one in none is Enhanced. Add one with `npx shadcn-nsh@latest add <name>`."],[1402,"Cross line"],[1089,"Current"],[1387,"Custom items"],[2129,"Customizing"],[660,"DataTable"],[680,"Date Picker"],[1628,"Decorative or not"],[1365,"Default `pair`: chevrons stacked at the end. `split`: − before the field and + after it."],[758,"Default chrome"],[403,"Defaults from `calendarLook` / `CalendarItem`. Every prop of `nsh/base` Calendar passes through."],[128,"Destructive"],[1644,"Detents"],[803,"Diagnostics"],[699,"Dialog"],[7,"diff"],[733,"DiffView"],[338,"Disabled"],[463,"Disabled"],[1067,"Disabled"],[1452,"Disabled"],[1497,"Disabled"],[1746,"Disabled"],[1835,"Disabled"],[2007,"Disabled"],[2034,"Disabled"],[580,"Disabled and clearable"],[1600,"Disabled choice, disabled select"],[65,"Disabled row"],[753,"Dockable workspace chrome for tabs, splits, and edge docks."],[752,"DockArea"],[769,"Drawer"],[1787,"Each column is a stack of its own, so pushing a page in the detail leaves the sidebar and the list where they are. `SplitViewSidebar` is the sidebar's fill (`colors.sidebar`) with a hairline of `colors.sidebarBorder` after it. `SplitViewContent` is the page's fill with `colors.line` after it. `SplitViewDetail` has no hairline. iOS draws the columns' own edges, so the hairlines are left out there."],[422,"Each part is the `nsh` element it is drawn with, wearing the look `cardLook()` gives it. Every\nview prop passes through; `style` goes over the look's."],[1853,"Each part of `fieldFamilyLook()` reads the theme when it is drawn, so a look kept in a `const` still follows the scheme."],[2287,"Edit the sources; every component follows. Change a brand color in `cssVars.light` and `cssVars.dark`, a radius in `cssVars.theme`, a shadow part in the DTCG `shadow` group, a gradient, style group or material in the theme's `tokens/` files. Keep the keys: components and finishes refer to them by name, and both appearances need the same merged finish shape — a finish you add states every field of its neighbours, and a value that follows the device is stated twice, `pointer` and `touch`, with the same keys — a theme that has its own device sizes writes them in `tokens/themes/<id>/pointer.tokens.json` and `touch.tokens.json`, and one that does not inherits the base set's."],[2141,"Edit the values and keep the keys: components and finishes refer to them by name, and both appearances need the same merged finish shape. This is the change that reaches every component at once. Theme lists the roles."],[796,"Editor"],[825,"Emoji picker"],[845,"Empty"],[2123,"Enhanced"],[881,"Errors"],[721,"Escape, a backdrop press and a downward swipe close the dialog; turn any of them off on the content."],[2167,"Every command takes `-c, --cwd <dir>` (default: the current directory). `init`, `add`, `list`, `view` and `diff` also take `--registry <url>`, a template with `{name}` in it. CLI has every flag and default."],[2389,"Every demo on this site can be drawn in any of these palettes: pick one with the **Demo theme**\nswitch in the nav, and the previews load again in it. The panel above is the showcase — buttons, a\ncard with a field, badges, switches, a slider and a progress bar, with the card, inset and press finishes\nthe palette brings. The list is `apps/website/demos/palettes.ts`. Each palette has its own page,\nwith the same sections: how to install it, every token it sets, and every finish it draws. Those\npages read each theme's `theme.json` and `semantics.json`, following the\ndesign-semantics standard\nand the theme roles spec."],[2258,"Every finish states a `foreground` — the ink that sits on it — so a component needs no fallback, and `shadow` names the parts of the theme's scale (`[\"{shadow.edge.surface}\", \"{shadow.sm}\"]`) instead of writing one: `elevation(\"md\")` gives the same values on its own. A theme that paints flat leaves `gradient` out and gets `null`, so the component draws no background image."],[1160,"Every part that draws a view takes `nsh`'s view props and spreads them on it after its own look, so an app's `testID`, `accessibilityLabel`, `onLongPress` or `class` reaches the row it passes them to; `style` goes over the look's, and the states an app passes (`hoverStyle`, `focusStyle`, `activeStyle`, `disabledStyle`) are merged after the look's own. `Menu` and `MenuSub` draw no view of their own (they own the open state and the trigger slot), so they take none: an app gives those props to the trigger or the content."],[1466,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Button passes through (`onPress`, `disabled`, `selected`, `role`, `hitSlop`, …). `style`, `hoverStyle`, `activeStyle` and `focusVisibleStyle` go over the look's. `scale` is the sink of a press."],[372,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Button passes through. `style`, `hoverStyle`, `activeStyle`, `focusVisibleStyle` and `disabledStyle` go over the look's."],[472,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Checkbox passes through. `indicatorClass` and `indicatorStyle` go over the look's. The row is the `group` the box sinks with while pressed."],[751,"Every prop of `nsh/base` DiffView passes through."],[809,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Editor passes through: the text (`value` / `defaultValue`, `onChange`), the language and its highlighting, folding, soft wrap, search, the editing keys and the diagnostics. The shell adds the look (`editorClasses`) and the surface (`editorFrame()`)."],[1002,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Input passes through. `class`, `style` and `disabledStyle` go over the look's. Focus and hover edges are classes on the look."],[1177,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Menu passes through on `MenubarContent`\nexcept the trigger, the open state and the lifecycle callbacks, which the root owns. `popupStyle`,\n`backdropStyle` and `popupStartingStyle` go over `menuPopup`'s. Defaults: `placement` `\"bottom\"`,\n`align` `\"start\"`, `offset` `8` — a menu under the trigger it belongs to, whatever the bar's width."],[1367,"Every prop of `nsh/base` NumberInput passes through. `class`, `inputStyle` and the step props go over the look's."],[1379,"Every prop of `nsh/base` OtpInput passes through. Cell and caret props go over the look's."],[1506,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Radio and `RadioGroup` passes through. Style props go over the look's. The row is the `group` the ring sinks with while pressed. `RadioGroupItem` is an alias of `Radio`."],[795,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Sheet passes through on `DrawerContent`\nexcept open state and the lifecycle callbacks, which the root owns. `popupStyle` and `backdropStyle`\ngo over the look's. Defaults: `side` `\"bottom\"`, `closeOnSwipe` `true`."],[1654,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Sheet passes through on `SheetContent`. `popupStyle` and `backdropStyle` go over the look's."],[1854,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Switch passes through. `trackClass`, `trackStyle` and `thumbStyle` go over the look's."],[1900,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Tabs / `Tab` passes through on the list and triggers."],[1918,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Terminal passes through, and so does\nits ref (`TerminalRef`): `write`, `reset`, `text`, `focus`. `class`, `style`, `cursorClass` and\n`cursorStyle` go over the look's, so an app gives the cursor its shape (`w-0.5`) and moves the\npadding where it needs another."],[1953,"Every prop of `nsh/base` TimeField passes through; `class`, `segmentClass`, `separatorStyle` and `renderSegment` go over the look's."],[1991,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Toast passes through. `style` goes over `toastLook`."],[2024,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Toggle and ToggleGroup passes through. `style`, `hoverStyle`, `activeStyle`, `focusVisibleStyle`, `pressedStyle` and `disabledStyle` go over the look's."],[2044,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Toolbar, `ToolbarGroup` and `ToolbarSeparator` passes through. `style` goes over the look's. Items keep their own look (`Button`, `Toggle`, …)."],[1738,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through (`style`, `accessibilityLabel`, …); `style` goes over the look's."],[167,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through (`style`, `accessibilityLabel`, `onPress`, …); `style` goes over the look's, so a caller's own width, corners or fill replace the look's and the box keeps its ratio inside them."],[1633,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through (`style`, `role`,\n`accessibilityLabel`, …); `style` goes over the look's."],[1079,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through (`style`, `role`, …); `style` goes over the look's."],[147,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through on `Alert` and\n`AlertDescription`, and every prop of `nsh` Text on `AlertTitle`;\n`style` goes over the look's on each. The root is `role=\"alert\"`, so a notice is read out when it\nappears."],[261,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through on `Breadcrumb`,\n`BreadcrumbList`, `BreadcrumbItem`, `BreadcrumbSeparator` and `BreadcrumbEllipsis`, and every prop\nof `nsh` Text on `BreadcrumbPage`; `BreadcrumbLink` is\n`nsh/base`'s Link with all its props (`href`, `openWith`, `onOpen`,\n`onPress`, `disabled`, `hitSlop`, …). Style props go over the look's."],[297,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through on `BubbleGroup`,\n`Bubble` and `BubbleContent`; `BubbleText` takes every prop of\n`nsh` Text, and `BubbleContent` draws a string child as a\n`BubbleText`. Style props go over the look's."],[868,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through on `Empty`,\n`EmptyHeader`, `EmptyMedia` and `EmptyContent`, and every prop of\n`nsh` Text on `EmptyTitle` and `EmptyDescription`; `style` goes\nover the look's on each."],[1120,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through on `Marker` and\n`MarkerIcon` (`role`, `onPress`, `accessibilityLabel`, …), and every prop of\n`nsh` Text on `MarkerContent`. Style props go over the look's:\n`style` on a `View` or `Text` part."],[1273,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through on `MessageGroup`,\n`Message` and `MessageContent` (`role`, `accessibilityLabel`, `style`, …). With no `children`,\n`MessageAvatar` is this library's `Avatar`: `name`, `src`,\n`fallback`, `onStatusChange` and the rest of its props pass through. With `children` it renders a\n`View` (`style`, `accessibilityLabel` and the other host props still pass through; `name`, `src`\nand the image props are not used). A string child of `MessageFooter` and of `MessageHeader` is\ndrawn as `nsh` Text."],[1227,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through on `MessageScroller` and\n`MessageScrollerItem`; `MessageScrollerViewport` takes a `List`'s\n(`keyExtractor`, `estimatedItemSize`, `onViewableItemsChange`, `scrollbar`, …) less the state the\nscroller keeps (`inverted`, `initialScrollIndex`, `initialScrollAtEnd`,\n`maintainVisibleContentPosition`, …), plus `each`, `alignment` and `onLoadMoreAtStart` (all passed to\nthe list — the last one loads older turns) and the child that renders a row; and `MessageScrollerButton` takes this library's\n`Button` props (`variant` defaults to `secondary`, `size` to\n`sm`). `alignment=\"bottom\"` pins a short conversation to the bottom of the viewport. `indicator`\nis a mark at the button's top-end corner (an arrival dot); the arrow stays."],[325,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through on all three parts;\n`style` goes over the look's on each."],[1978,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through on all three, and `style`\ngoes over the look's on `TitleBar` and `WindowControls`."],[1059,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through on both parts (`style`, `accessibilityLabel`, …); `style` goes over the look's."],[503,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through on every part but `CodeBlockTitle` (a `nsh` Text), `CodeBlockCopyButton` (an `IconButton`) and `CodeBlockContent` (a `nsh` Scroll); `style` goes over the look's. The text of the code is selectable."],[2091,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through on every part but `TraceTitle` and `TraceDescription` (a `nsh` Text), `TraceCollapsible` (the props below) and `TraceCollapsibleContent` (`nsh/base`'s Collapsible); `style` goes over the look's."],[191,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through on every part;\n`AttachmentAction` takes this library's `Button` props,\n`AttachmentTrigger` the view's (`onPress`, `accessibilityLabel`, `disabled`, …), and\n`AttachmentTitle`/`AttachmentDescription` the text's. A title or a description is one line,\ntruncated."],[47,"Every registry file the CLI fetches over HTTP is kept in `~/.cache/shadcn-nsh` (`$XDG_CACHE_HOME`, or `SHADCN_NSH_CACHE_DIR` when set). Offline, `diff` compares with those copies and says when they were fetched; the public registry's URL is pinned to the CLI's release, so they are that registry exactly. With no copy, it prints `diff skipped` and exits `2`, so a check can tell \"could not check\" from \"differs\":"],[1572,"Every scroll view"],[2,"Every shadcn-nsh@latest command, with its flags and defaults."],[649,"Every shadcn/ui component and every NSH element, and what this library has for it."],[525,"Every trigger but the `first` draws a divider above it, inside its row, so the hover fill meets the line; `start` lines the trigger and the panel up past a leading icon. A row in the panel (`listRow`) reaches past the content, and the revealed region clips it, so give the panel room on both sides: `panel={{ start: 12, end: 12 }}`."],[903,"Every view prop passes through the parts drawn as views, and every text prop the parts drawn as\ntexts. `style` goes over the look's, so a width or a gap on a part wins."],[1039,"Every view prop passes through the parts drawn as views