h/base` Progress passes through.\nThe rail is the theme's track form: a sunk groove 6 points high with the inset shade, an accent-tinted\nband 4 points high, or WinUI's 1-point input line under a 3-point run; `height` overrides the height,\nnever the form."],[1576,"Uses `scrollbarTheme` by default. Call `Scrollbar.setTheme()` to install it on every scroll view. Every prop of `nsh/base` Scrollbar passes through."],[1589,"Uses `segmentedLook`. Composition: `Segmented`, `SegmentedList`, `SegmentedItem`. Every prop of `nsh/base` Tabs / `Tab` passes through on the list and items."],[2115,"Uses `treeItemClass` and `TreeRow` by default. Every prop of `nsh/base` Tree passes through."],[1748,"Value column"],[235,"Variant"],[336,"Variant"],[482,"Variant"],[986,"Variant"],[1014,"Variant"],[2005,"Variant"],[1375,"Verdict"],[1533,"Vertical"],[1749,"Vertical"],[2009,"Vertical"],[2035,"Vertical"],[877,"Vertical and horizontal"],[6,"view"],[1271,"What a reply carries under it is the app's: a copy that flips to a check for a moment, and two\nthumbs. `IconButton` takes `selected`, so a pressed thumb shows the brand ink and reports\n`accessibilityState={{ selected: true }}`; the rating itself is only the app's state until the app\nsends it."],[1332,"What a trigger opens"],[2176,"When developing this repository:"],[953,"When to use a group, and when an `Input`"],[814,"Where the bar is and whether it is open are the app's: it sits beside the editor in the same `View`\nrather than inside it, since a part cannot leave the tree. The keys are the app's too — Escape and\n`mod+f` belong to its `keymap`, as a part that captured them would take them from the editor while\nthe bar is closed. Because the search is one object, a query the app sets — from\n`onFindWithSelection`, or from a keybinding — reads in the bar, and the bar's edits move the\neditor's matches as it types."],[1841,"Where the numbers come from"],[1790,"Where the window is horizontally compact, one column shows: the first that `